<!--
    The IEEE 68-bus, 16-machine system with a meshed four-terminal DC grid: complements ieee68-dc.xiidm (Ieee68DcNetwork.create,
    flat).

    The machines PST's data16m.m's (MIT licence, (c) Joe Chow / Cherry Tree Scientific Software), on their own rating: H, Xd, Xq,
    X'd, X'q, X''d = X''q, Xl, T'd0, T''d0, T'q0 and T''q0, subtransient all of them, unsaturated (the data's saturation left
    out). Ours where the data give none or the model wants another: an armature resistance of 0.003 pu, as Ieee39DcNetwork's;
    G53's q axis, the data's hydro unit with no X''q and T'q0 0.035 s - its one q winding a subtransient one, X''q its X''d,
    T''q0 0.035 s, and the transient one all but absent, 0.99 Xq and ten times its T''q0, as Ieee39DcNetwork's G30; the area
    equivalents' damping, G65 to G68, the data's d_o. Their exciters the data's static ones (exc_con, type 0): the simplified AVR,
    a gain of 100 within +-5 pu of field voltage, a 10 ms lag. The PSSs of G53 to G64 the data's (pss_con, speed input): a gain of
    50 to 110, a 10 s washout, two lead-lags; their output within +-0.2 pu, where the data have -0.05 to 0.2 (one limit here).
    The data give no governor: each machine on a TGOV1, ours, as Ieee39DcNetwork's: R 5 %, T1 0.5 s, the valve within 0 and 1 pu,
    T2 3 s, T3 10 s, no Dt.

    The DC grid's converters averaged as Ieee39DcNetwork's, a 15 % phase reactor on their rating (R 0.003 pu), DC capacitors of
    40 ms, a bridge inductance for their blocking, grid-following: CS16 on the DC voltage, CS33, CS41 and CS52 on their DC voltage
    droop, as IIDM's control mode says. Each DC line one lumped pi of its 400 kV conductor: 2 L and C / 2 of CIGRE B4's +-200 kV
    per-km OHL pole data (0.8273 mH, 0.0139 uF).
-->
